    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, whose elite speed profile and favorable matchup against Dobbins propel him to an 81.26, the highest score on the roster. The combination of his leadoff spot and a dynamic platoon advantage makes him our primary weapon to secure the scarcest category: stolen bases. Joining him at the top of the projected performance bracket are **Yordan Alvarez** (65.52) and **Junior Caminero** (62.27). Despite facing the lefty Rogers, **Junior Caminero** remains a must-start due to his high-leverage spot in the three-hole, while **Yordan Alvarez** continues to provide high-floor production, with his elite 0.465 xwOBA effectively insulating him against any concern regarding the matchup with Woo.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Caleb Durbin**, who landed just outside our active rotation with a 48.55 score. While **Caleb Durbin** benefits from a slow opposing pitcher delivery\u2014which is a green light for our stolen base strategy\u2014the optimizer favored the higher raw power profiles of **Pedro Ramirez** and **Kazuma Okamoto** in the middle infield and corner spots. **Gary Sanchez** remains the most precarious start of the day; his 41.24 rating is heavily depressed by the presence of Skubal, an elite arm with a 2.77 xERA. While we are starting him to maintain our daily game cap efficiency, we are closely monitoring the risk of a sub-optimal offensive performance. Otherwise, the lineup is well-positioned to capitalize on the favorable parks and situational order advantages provided by **Kyle Schwarber** leading off and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** anchoring the middle of the order.",
